From 80c366fbd6cb3cfa323671a4dc927517094cf034 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:57:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09363/11362] Record submission 55657962 (kernel v40, read-only
 store fix)

The --submit-only path updated kernel_version but appended no history row, so
the record stopped at v37. This adds the entry, with what changed against the
0.02 submission, what deliberately did not, and the one open question this
submission does NOT address.

Also records why the local gate's earlier solved-0 / timed_out-8 result on the
same day must not be read as a regression: that run shared the box with a
two-GPU A/B. On a quiet box the same gate solves 7 of 8 with three bonus solves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
